---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Sources and Updates: Stranger Than Heaven Tracker"
  description="Every source behind this Stranger Than Heaven site, what each one is used for, how the pre-release achievement list is handled, and a log of changes."
  path="/sources/"
>
  <h1>Sources and updates</h1>
  <p class="lede">Where each fact comes from, and what has changed on the site.</p>

  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Used for</th><th scope="col">Checked</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {site.sources.map((source) => (
          <tr id={source.id}>
            <td><a href={source.url}>{source.name}</a></td>
            <td>{source.use}</td>
            <td style="white-space:nowrap">{source.checked}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How facts are handled</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <ul>
      <li>Official statements from SEGA, RGG Studio, Xbox and the store pages come first.</li>
      <li>Where an outlet is the source, it is named beside the fact.</li>
      <li>Nothing is copied: descriptions and achievement requirements are restated in our own words. Achievement names are given as reported, because they are names.</li>
      <li>What has not been announced is listed as unannounced, not guessed.</li>
      <li>No game artwork, screenshots or trailer stills are used.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>The achievement list</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The list did not come from an announcement. Overnight on 8 and 9 September 2026, achievement data for dozens
      of unreleased Steam games turned out to be readable through Steam's API, and the tracking site Exophase, which
      scans Steam automatically, recorded it. Its owner put that down to a mistake on Valve's side. SEGA has not
      confirmed or denied the list.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is used here because it was published widely the same day, and because a checklist is only useful if it is
      complete. It is labelled as pre-release on every page that uses it, and it will be checked against the released
      game in launch week.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <ul>
    {site.changelog.map((entry) => (
      <li><strong>{entry.date}:</strong> {entry.text}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</Base>
